; exclude_index_out_of_range: EXCLUDE writes a coefficient and must bound it.
;
; ISA.md placed no bound on these indices until the spec said which
; behaviour was right. It now says IndexOutOfBounds, for consistency with
; every other model-writing opcode, and this vector holds the VM to it.
;
; The failure this rules out is the expensive one: a VM that does not
; check would insert quad(2, 100) on a model whose variables are 0..4, so
; the mutual-exclusion constraint the program asked for would be attached
; to a variable that does not exist. It would constrain nothing, the model
; would solve cleanly, and nothing in the output would distinguish it from
; a correct run.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 2           ; i, in range
PUSH 100         ; j, far past the extent
PUSH 1           ; penalty
EXCLUDE r0
HALT
